    "result_text": "The full suite (one real test class, `AcceptanceTest`) passes and the project compiles clean. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (global sequence) to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a **per-city** sequence.\n\n**Format logic** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`\n- Now builds `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`: CITY3 = upper-cased first 3 letters of city, LAST3 = upper-cased first 3 of last name, NNNN = `countByCity(city) + 1` (one more than owners already in that city).\n- Extracted a small private `prefix(String)` helper so the city/last-name three-letter logic isn't duplicated.\n\n**Per-city count** \u2014 the sequence needs \"owners already in that city,\" which no repository method provided, so I added `long countByCity(String city)`:\n- `repository/OwnerRepository.java` \u2014 interface method + javadoc, next to `count()`.\n- `springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java` \u2014 `@Query` counting by city (this is the active profile in tests).\n- `jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` and `jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` \u2014 mirrored implementations following each impl's existing `count()` style.\n\n**Derived values** \u2014 `AssignMembershipNumber` reads `owner.getCustomerCode()` at runtime, so the membership number (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) automatically rebuilds on the new format; no code change was needed there. I confirmed nothing else derives from `customerCode` (`householdId` is assigned earlier in the pipeline).\n\n**Docs** \u2014 updated `openapi.yml` description/examples for `customerCode` (`LON-SMI-0007`) and `membershipNumber` (`LON-SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) passes; `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures.",
